Dependabot:
  GitHub's Dependabot is an example of a proactive security measure. Dependabot constantly monitors newly published CVEs, and whenever a linked library becomes
  vulnerable, it sends out an alert to inform you there is a new vulnerability that needs to be patched.
OWASP ZAP:
  OWASP ZAP is a proactive security measure because it automatically scans web applications while they are being developed. This means that developers get feedback on
  the security of their projects while they are being written, preventing vulnerabilities ever being exposed to the public.
OSS-Fuzz:
  OSS-Fuzz continuously tests open-source software for vulnerabilities by throwing large amounts of malformed inputs at the software to see what makes it crash/ what
  security bugs there are. This is proactive because it finds the vulnerabilities before an attacker can.
